		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://fffff.at/?p=3641#comment-10855</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[This doesn&#039;t resolve any of the questions left from the last episode!

Also, I don&#039;t think my data is a bike. If my data was a bike only one person could use it at a time. That&#039;s basically the same argument the RIAA uses to argue against file sharing.

I share my data with lots of entities, and it&#039;s still my data. If Google uses my data to work in a way I don&#039;t like, that&#039;s just my fault for not reading the TOS. Ultimately, the thing that is precious isn&#039;t the data itself but the association with and control of that data. If Google started impersonating or misrepresenting me, then there&#039;s really an issue.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This doesn&#8217;t resolve any of the questions left from the last episode!</p>
<p>Also, I don&#8217;t think my data is a bike. If my data was a bike only one person could use it at a time. That&#8217;s basically the same argument the RIAA uses to argue against file sharing.</p>
<p>I share my data with lots of entities, and it&#8217;s still my data. If Google uses my data to work in a way I don&#8217;t like, that&#8217;s just my fault for not reading the TOS. Ultimately, the thing that is precious isn&#8217;t the data itself but the association with and control of that data. If Google started impersonating or misrepresenting me, then there&#8217;s really an issue.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
